    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Description\n\nI had another feature request about mini.completion. \r\nIs it possible to set border configuration for the wildmenu used by mini.completion?\r\nIf not can it be integrated into mini.completion in any way? \r\nIf that is not possible, can you suggest some hacky way in which I can get borders around it.\nAlso does mini.completion wildmenu color not change according to mini.hues and mini.base16?",
